    "temperature": {
      "file": "cooling_tower_basin_temperature.glb",
      "title": "The basin holds the coldest water in the loop",
      "description": "Hot return water (e.g. 40 °C) is cooled mainly by evaporation in the fill and rain zone and collects in the basin at the cold-water temperature (e.g. 30 °C; range 10 °C, approach to wet-bulb ≈ 3–5 °C). Evaporation (≈ 0.15 % of flow per °C of range) concentrates the dissolved solids, so blowdown keeps cycles of concentration ≈ 3–6, and make-up = evaporation + drift + blowdown. The sump depth gives the pumps submergence against vortices.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
